  Design note: accounting is independent of authentication.  The TFS says so: "User
  login accounting is separate from user login authentication. When a user logs in,
  regardless of what authentication method was used, the user login accounting will
  behave as per its configuration."  This case therefore left
  "aaa authentication login default local" alone throughout.  "manager" kept working on
  every path, so no escape account was needed.  It also means every record below was
  produced for a LOCALLY authenticated login.

